window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Vampires killed my parents—now I won’t stop until I get my revenge.</b></p> <p>Three years training to kill wayward vampires, and it’s finally graduation day. I’ll be leading an elite team, assembled by the royal vampire queen herself. </p> <p>Everything is going according to plan until I meet <i>him</i>. </p> <p>Ransom is charming, witty, and sexy, but he’s also the worst thing—a vampire. </p> <p>My enemy. </p> <p>Our connection is undeniable, but I refuse to succumb. </p> <p>But there are rebel vampires after the queen’s throne, which risks humans, shifters, and vampires alike. The only way to ensure our safety and get my revenge is to team up with him. </p> <p>If I don’t kill him first. </p> <p><b>This is an upper YA/NA crossover with schmexy, sinful vampires and is best suited for ages 17+. Be warned this is a slow burn enemies-to-lovers romance, and the steaminess factor does increase through the course of the series!</b></p> <p><b>Vampish is set within the world of Azar, along with (in listening order) </b><b><i>Hitched</i></b><b>, </b><b><i>Darkblood Academy</i></b><b>, </b><b><i>Royally Hitched</i></b><b>, </b><b><i>Darkblood Prison</i></b><b>, and </b><b><i>Wolfish</i></b><b>, but it's not necessary to listen to the other series first to enjoy this one.</b></p>"; 
